WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.209
Promise versus Delivery.

00:00:02.159 --> 00:00:04.659
What they said versus what happened.

00:00:04.659 --> 00:00:09.329
Every major government program promise mapped against the actual delivery outcome.

00:00:09.329 --> 00:00:13.636
Pharmacare: promised universal, delivered two drug categories.

00:00:13.636 --> 00:00:17.670
Dental care: promised universal, got provider opt-outs.

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:21.568
Childcare: promised ten dollars a day, got waitlists.

00:00:21.568 --> 00:00:26.852
Foreign interference registry: promised accountability, got zero registrations.

00:00:26.852 --> 00:00:30.931
Passport processing: promised twenty days, delivered months.

00:00:30.931 --> 00:00:33.920
MAID: promised safeguards, removed them.

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:37.022
Every comparison from official government records.

00:00:37.022 --> 00:00:40.295
The pattern is consistent across every program.

00:00:40.295 --> 00:00:42.943
Promise a transformational programme.

00:00:42.943 --> 00:00:45.170
Set aggressive timelines.

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:48.693
Underfund or understaff the delivery infrastructure.

00:00:48.693 --> 00:00:52.193
Measure success by announcements, not outcomes.

00:00:52.193 --> 00:00:58.613
When the gap between promise and delivery becomes undeniable, blame complexity, provinces, or the previous government.

00:00:58.613 --> 00:01:01.079
Never hold anyone accountable.

00:01:01.079 --> 00:01:03.340
This is not incompetence.

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:07.022
It is the institutional architecture functioning as designed.
